# Every Flyway migration, pinned by SHA-256 (src/backend/CLAUDE.md § Migrations). scripts/validate_migration_versions.py
# holds each migration file to its line, so changing a migration's bytes needs a readable one-line diff here to go
# green — in the same commit as the change.
#
# Why: Flyway validates the checksum of every applied migration at start, so an edited migration fails startup on
# every instance that already ran it. Until the first release, a baseline may still change, but only together with
# its pin line, so the change cannot go unnoticed. From the release on, a migration at or below the released
# version is never edited — not even a comment — only followed by a new one.
#
# `release:` names the highest migration version the first release ships, or `none` while no release exists. Only
# the owner declares a release; the guard cannot know when one happens.
#
# Format: `<sha256>  <repo-relative path>`, one line per migration, in ascending version order. A new migration
# appends its line in the commit that adds it, and its version must be above every line before it (Flyway runs
# outOfOrder=false: an existing instance refuses a migration below its current version).
release: none
